<section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-5">
  <p>
    "Get a job." "Sort out the estate." "Learn to swim." These are the things
    that actually matter, and they're also the things that sit untouched for
    a year, because none of them is a task — each is a fog with a task
    somewhere inside it.
  </p>
  <p>
    The gap between an ambition and a first step is where most people's
    plans die, and closing it is one of the few things a model is
    unambiguously good at.
  </p>
</section>

<%= about_screenshot("tasks") %>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">How it goes</h2>
  <ol class="mt-6 space-y-4">
    <li class="card p-5">
      <h3 class="font-semibold">1 · You say the big thing in one line</h3>
      <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-soft">
        In your own words, without structuring it. "I need to sort out mum's
        house." That sentence is the entire input.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="card p-5">
      <h3 class="font-semibold">2 · It comes back as steps</h3>
      <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-soft">
        Each one small enough to finish inside a day, in a sensible order,
        with dates on the ones that genuinely have them. Yours to edit,
        delete and reorder — it's a first draft, not an instruction.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="card p-5">
      <h3 class="font-semibold">3 · They join everything else</h3>
      <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-soft">
        Not into a separate project app. Onto the same board as the bins and
        the dentist, because that's the list you actually look at.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">The board</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Later") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Everything you've said you'll do. Allowed to be long — that's what
        it's for.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Today") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        What you've claimed for today. Deliberately a decision you make,
        rather than a list the software assigns you.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Done") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Kept visible, because on the days when nothing feels finished, the
        evidence that things were is worth having.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">The situations, not just the goals</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    Some things aren't a goal so much as a period of life happening to you —
    a bereavement, a redundancy, a move, becoming someone's carer. Those
    produce work across half the app at once, and they're handled the same
    way: one sentence in, and a plan out whose steps land wherever they
    belong.
  </p>
</section>
